<spell-notebook "nag theming">
	<header level="1">
		Nag
		<header>A nag is a persistent message that stays until dismissed, and can remember the dismissal.</>
	</>
	<nag-tab-bar showing="theming"/>
	<section>
		<html>
			<ui-menu class="ui-docs-section-tabs" appearance="segmented" aria-label="Sections">
				<ui-item link="#tokens">Tokens</>
				<ui-item link="#themes">Themes</>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<!-- THEMING:  the family's tokens, live, plus how to set them and which themes touch it. -->
	<section label="Tokens">
		<markdown>
			Theme with the public `--ui-nag-*` tokens: set one on the element, on any ancestor (`:root` for every nag), or
			on the bar through `::part(nag)`. They inherit into the shadow root, where the sheet reads each through a
			private alias, so nothing inside blocks them. `inverted` reads the `--ui-nag-inverted-*` tokens instead. Style
			the close icon with `::part(close)`.
		</>
		<markdown>
			```css
			/* every nag on the page */
			ui-nag {
			  --ui-nag-padding: 1em 2em;
			}
			/* the close icon */
			ui-nag::part(close) {
			  opacity: 1;
			}
			```
		</>
		<message state="info" size="small">
			<markdown>
				Fomantic's grey bar with dark text and a white title (3.2:1 contrast) is a dark grey bar with light text here.
				Never set the `--_ui-nag-*` names: they're the sheet's private plumbing.
			</>
		</>
		<markdown>Edit a value below to try it.</>
		<html>
			<ui-docs-tokens family="ui-nag" playground>
				<ui-nag>
					<span class="title">We have updated our privacy policy.</>
				</>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Themes">
		<markdown>
			The theme menu above picks the theme for every page of the site:  Spell, Glass, Fruity or Merlot,
			each restyling this component through its tokens.
		</>
	</>
</spell-notebook>
